Read `.claude/skills/realtime-tempo/SKILL.md` in full before changing anything
in `Source/AI/` or `Source/Tracking/`. It is the single source of truth for the
tempo chain and it is shared with Claude Code and Codex - update it there, not
here.

Non-negotiables it spells out:

- ONNX never runs on the audio thread; the musical clock never leaves it.
- No allocation, no locks, no I/O in `process` / `advance` / `render`.
- The clock never restarts because the BPM changed - a tempo change is a rate
  change, never a re-anchor.
- Never take the beat's tempo *or its position* from a single onset or a volume
  spike.
- Every hypothesis is projected to "now" by
  `(numSamples - offset)/sampleRate + reportedLatencyMs*0.001` before it reaches
  the clock. If you add a new evidence source, project it the same way.
- Phase time constants are in **seconds**, never a per-block blend - a fixed
  blend makes the constant a function of buffer size.
- The octave (half/double time) is not fully solvable from the signal. Do not
  "fix" it in the decoder; AUTO plus the listener's choice is the design.

Verify with `./scripts/run-tests.sh` plus the probe targets listed in the skill
(`VPAlign`, `VPBar`, `VPTiming`, `VPProbe`, `VPRoom`, `VPReplay`). A timing
change with no probe number attached is not reviewable.
